## Scope & Methodology

This audit evaluated the device configuration listed above against the Agent-Assisted Coding controls framework (`controls.yaml` v{{ ctx.controls_version }}), covering the Agent-Assisted Coding 3-plane hardening model (management, control, and data plane) and the Cisco IOS-XE hardening practices it encodes. Controls without a mapped external CIS Cisco IOS-XE Benchmark section are cited by their Agent-Assisted Coding control ID only; no CIS section reference is claimed unless a real mapping has been supplied for that control.

Deterministic controls were evaluated automatically against the device's running configuration. Controls marked "Manual Review" require human judgment (e.g. banner wording against corporate legal policy) and are listed separately below rather than auto-scored. Findings already covered by a documented exception are still listed in Findings Detail, marked accordingly, rather than silently excluded.

**Out of scope:** physical security, change-management process compliance, and any control outside the Agent-Assisted Coding framework's current 17 controls.

